 and patient understanding"}, {"id": "b63de1a6-d74f-4da0-a9ad-0e81f5612978", "type": "concept", "title": "Portal adoption and support"}]}, {"id": "58732fd7-b3c1-4a24-8b9b-6c243dd0806d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Wearables and consumer data", "description": "Consumer-generated data can help or mislead care decisions.", "children": [{"id": "194d28f5-b618-4d91-9638-64f3c8d9c944", "type": "concept", "title": "Fitness trackers, ECG wearables, sleep and activity data"}, {"id": "78f8ce8b-2772-4719-a11a-cf42b6c8ed99", "type": "concept", "title": "Signal versus noise"}, {"id": "8a347caa-2de1-4218-9523-e459535d4864", "type": "concept", "title": "Documentation and clinical responsibility"}]}]}, {"id": "865b957d-194f-4e8d-a060-d873e56e4d3d", "type": "topic", "title": "Health Data Analytics, Dashboards, and Quality Improvement", "description": "Students learn to use dashboards and data displays to identify patterns, monitor outcomes, and drive quality improvement.", "children": [{"id": "400f53da-0477-4c5d-8558-29708e78f06f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Analytics foundations", "description": "Students learn how clinical data become measures.", "children": [{"id": "c4759d70-479f-476b-b254-4e027da95b65", "type": "concept", "title": "Descriptive, diagnostic, predictive, and prescriptive analytics"}, {"id": "67c18c9e-ac0f-4916-9e2a-a6978e1a3613", "type": "concept", "title": "Cohorts, denominators, numerators, and risk adjustment"}, {"id": "58d7ef69-1ba1-4846-b4b7-6bf8a54ec874", "type": "concept", "title": "Run charts and basic trend interpretation"}]}, {"id": "13f79ab2-c95f-43a0-b86b-be6248306dfb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dashboards", "description": "Dashboards should support action, not decoration.", "children": [{"id": "fcce1e29-0130-48b0-acec-a36fc3b20cf1", "type": "concept", "title": "Quality, safety, staffing, throughput, and outcome dashboards"}, {"id": "24307ea0-ff03-4acf-933d-5b7369710c2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Drilldowns, thresholds, and visual clarity"}, {"id": "2418ffc1-283e-4346-8316-ce0d1069be13", "type": "concept", "title": "Data latency and measure definitions"}]}, {"id": "65845dd7-0bb8-497e-83c9-cc69dd81c43a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Quality improvement with data", "description": "Students connect informatics to better care.", "children": [{"id": "6a19c80e-d85f-4598-be2b-0d094616fdce", "type": "concept", "title": "PDSA cycles"}, {"id": "d180f504-5c7f-49bf-b289-d02f0eb12ba9", "type": "concept", "title": "Clinical variation and process measures"}, {"id": "025b1f3d-9c03-4099-8128-a095c8dd78a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Outcome monitoring and sustainment"}]}]}, {"id": "6facbccd-b5f4-44d0-be2a-b82e310eda3b", "type": "topic", "title": "Workflow Design, Human Factors, Usability, and Safety", "description": "This topic teaches students to evaluate whether technology fits clinical work, reduces burden, and supports safe human performance.", "children": [{"id": "297a4757-0009-4d3d-948f-6b43ea732133", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Workflow analysis", "description": "Technology must be designed around real clinical work.", "children": [{"id": "a6d9709b-0c9a-4d9b-9119-2a0b0f1db0bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Current-state and future-state workflow maps"}, {"id": "41763fca-2563-4e77-ae79-64cc82a53892", "type": "concept", "title": "Handoffs, interruptions, queues, and workarounds"}, {"id": "1a6f4aa5-0727-48e3-9cdf-2e45525b7a93", "type": "concept", "title": "Shadowing and stakeholder interviews"}]}, {"id": "4698b6cc-d610-4e74-82d4-06c4a78272ba", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Human factors", "description": "Students learn how systems shape attention, memory, and error.", "children": [{"id": "44c67012-4649-4f19-a160-f4fdf316a870", "type": "concept", "title": "Cognitive load and alarm burden"}, {"id": "61bfa6d6-ad3d-496e-9b22-dd2399cd5066", "type": "concept", "title": "Standardization and forcing functions"}, {"id": "f848b68a-69cf-4e09-b141-c66fae127538", "type": "concept", "title": "Interface design and usability heuristics"}]}, {"id": "5e29e01b-2806-4df0-94be-69b9028c61e2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Safety evaluation", "description": "Good technology is monitored after go-live.", "children": [{"id": "5e47b521-bed4-494e-9d01-6e55aca2b7e1", "type": "concept", "title": "Usability testing"}, {"id": "f5cf7361-2787-4675-aeef-113b7d44ae40", "type": "concept", "title": "Hazard analysis and safety cases"}, {"id": "5ca84e18-754a-4d89-96bf-005b656859cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Incident reporting and learning systems"}]}]}, {"id": "d091ff16-d13b-4a74-8d4b-ac36ad3b3a20", "type": "topic", "title": "Public Health Informatics, Surveillance, and Population Health", "description": "Students connect clinical data to public health reporting, surveillance, community health, and population-level decision making.", "children": [{"id": "0a4ae6be-fa46-4e39-9f24-94bbc47b60cb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Public health data systems", "description": "Clinical data supports community-level action when governed and interpreted well.", "children": [{"id": "9a9d8ca2-2c54-497c-8739-649b44d168fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Registries, immunization systems, electronic case reporting"}, {"id": "56a31f7b-1e9c-4942-9161-954566b5d886", "type": "concept", "title": "CDC and public health data sources"}, {"id": "28b631b3-28b7-4694-a310-214c9c48a494", "type": "concept", "title": "Data modernization and surveillance"}]}, {"id": "e998f1c3-7980-4edd-8ce0-f244f8896f5b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Population health analytics", "description": "Students learn to see patterns beyond individual encounters.", "children": [{"id": "537f2d46-477d-4db0-a8ee-9bae2bc6275f", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk stratification"}, {"id": "4a9b6328-7b9d-4fc2-813b-a01d0ba51243", "type": "concept", "title": "Social determinants of health"}, {"id": "c301f7f7-c43e-4d05-93c6-dc1d41f4e56f", "type": "concept", "title": "Care gaps and outreach lists"}]}, {"id": "3e38ebc2-dae1-4353-948e-18c4dfe76ddc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Geographic and community data", "description": "Place matters in health.", "children": [{"id": "6618cb83-f4f9-434b-8fff-e83da90d109e", "type": "concept", "title": "GIS awareness"}, {"id": "611c573b-2945-4a44-a600-bc326f360500", "type": "concept", "title": "Community needs and resource mapping"}, {"id": "60b9d68e-0c0e-43ce-8254-a484f185be10", "type": "concept", "title": "Equity-focused population measures"}]}]}, {"id": "23bbf10f-cbbd-4cc4-9520-4111e759ca81", "type": "topic", "title": "AI, Algorithms, Bias, and Responsible Healthcare Technology", "description": "Students learn to evaluate AI and machine learning tools for transparency, bias, safety, accountability, and clinical fit.", "children": [{"id": "6e79483f-2e1e-452f-8760-4822613302b8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "AI and machine learning basics", "description": "Students learn enough to ask good clinical and ethical questions.", "children": [{"id": "a100981c-e007-40e3-9152-ce5e13792cc1", "type": "concept", "title": "Prediction, classification, natural language processing, generative AI"}, {"id": "a2c02c54-5f81-47a7-be05-15fd47d83399", "type": "concept", "title": "Training data and model validation"}, {"id": "f500a3bf-57c1-475d-ae52-bee0c3cad956", "type": "concept", "title": "Model performance and monitoring"}]}, {"id": "5c586725-38e5-4b67-b810-c3a43f023e33", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Bias and fairness", "description": "Algorithms can reproduce inequity when data or workflows are biased.", "children": [{"id": "f44f13c5-d79f-428f-aebd-d5c157674089", "type": "concept", "title": "Dataset bias and label bias"}, {"id": "eb0c7566-6ad0-40eb-90d3-0c4d8f16ec04", "type": "concept", "title": "False positives and false negatives across groups"}, {"id": "ea7193db-291b-4764-b15b-3f3ff969f301", "type": "concept", "title": "Fairness, transparency, and local validation"}]}, {"id": "ceb26c03-706a-4033-b698-471ece82c0b5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Responsible use", "description": "Nurses need practical guardrails for AI-enabled tools.", "children": [{"id": "c6166069-3992-4d12-b66c-6213b629e4b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Human oversight and scope of use"}, {"id": "9b625ea5-23f2-4447-aa43-1b3697bec410", "type": "concept", "title": "Documentation and disclosure"}, {"id": "c9ead61c-fec8-4e3a-ab23-09aef6dbb822", "type": "concept", "title": "Governance, accountability, and incident review"}]}]}, {"id": "d47c0d7f-132c-4153-bccf-7f1f3390c0ee", "type": "topic", "title": "Technology Implementation, Change Management, and Project Leadership", "description": "This module shows how health technology succeeds through stakeholder engagement, training, workflow integration, governance, and evaluation.", "children": [{"id": "653d0357-a015-4deb-9653-d58c041edbbb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Implementation lifecycle", "description": "Students learn what happens before, during, and after go-live.", "children": [{"id": "89693cfe-9a4b-413c-b594-f17f05749603", "type": "concept", "title": "Needs assessment, selection, build, testing, training, go-live, optimization"}, {"id": "5f44c76c-87b8-4a71-ab69-18e3ba1336a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Super users and command centers"}, {"id": "88fd00e0-b429-4961-8717-13eff0005d28", "type": "concept", "title": "Downtime and rollback planning"}]}, {"id": "627218d7-a5d9-4c98-b6d7-3243b4061f34", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Change management", "description": "Adoption is clinical, social, and organizational.", "children": [{"id": "bfceb200-066f-4616-bcb3-cca0c6c53ea6", "type": "concept", "title": "Stakeholder mapping"}, {"id": "81a58e29-520f-414c-aaa6-b4a5267b8d18", "type": "concept", "title": "Communication and training"}, {"id": "6d444fd1-bb7d-4dd9-b92f-7eea27f72a4e", "type": "concept", "title": "Resistance, feedback, and workflow redesign"}]}, {"id": "5a921f43-9954-438f-866f-a85458fde3d9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Project leadership", "description": "Nurses contribute essential clinical reality to health IT projects.", "children": [{"id": "31a27c26-d7de-46cc-b719-8a030ab649d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Scope, timeline, risks, and dependencies"}, {"id": "767579a1-c200-42ad-888d-5daf2c985b54", "type": "concept", "title": "Requirements and acceptance testing"}, {"id": "f3f75b84-1aaf-427b-b494-0bd844e3dbac", "type": "concept", "title": "Benefits realization and post-implementation review"}]}]}, {"id": "09c8453a-eb85-4cb1-ac8f-448e77befa85", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital Health Equity, Accessibility, and Inclusive Technology", "description": "Students learn to assess whether technology expands access or deepens disparities across language, disability, broadband, geography, and trust.", "children": [{"id": "2701ce01-9dd3-4ffc-8980-40b2aa0d1530", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital divide", "description": "Students learn how technology access shapes care access.", "children": [{"id": "81f61f98-3ddc-4ce9-b7ee-dc2cc63a71b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Broadband, devices, digital literacy, and language"}, {"id": "207a6160-ce44-4501-a10e-7f80b17e701b", "type": "concept", "title": "Rural access and disability access"}, {"id": "b1bb6ace-c598-486b-a483-810a7108f452", "type": "concept", "title": "Proxy access and caregiver support"}]}, {"id": "4e9f6b85-fea1-4cc4-9c4c-934d834f7bf0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accessible design", "description": "Health technology should work for diverse patients and clinicians.", "children": [{"id": "082ce836-5d70-4e18-ae69-fca14ca5aa1e", "type": "concept", "title": "Plain language and health literacy"}, {"id": "e41d8081-1645-4ade-b80b-fbb87cfbbca5", "type": "concept", "title": "Assistive technologies and inclusive UX"}, {"id": "55c177bc-8e14-4e27-9970-7442be328cc3", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural humility and trust"}]}, {"id": "408cd85e-0a67-4e2b-8ee0-0052cf969a20", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Equity evaluation", "description": "Technology should be assessed for unequal effects.", "children": [{"id": "661b6bf9-6b15-4e48-834c-3a79ba13d8a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Adoption gaps"}, {"id": "cd86bac5-bf41-42a6-ad9a-237e9cd8ffab", "type": "concept", "title": "Outcome differences by population"}, {"id": "17783e62-8033-4f67-8135-639708f88931", "type": "concept", "title": "Equity dashboards and mitigation plans"}]}]}, {"id": "07d01307-e322-4715-a7e0-6b270ca3628d", "type": "topic", "title": "Nursing Informatics Capstone: Technology Impact Evaluation", "description": "The course culminates in an applied informatics project evaluating a healthcare technology against safety, workflow, equity, data, and outcomes criteria.", "children": [{"id": "fb1f2e59-0a0a-421d-943d-d8ede10a3cf5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Problem framing", "description": "Students choose a real clinical technology problem and define the decision clearly.", "children": [{"id": "df8f770d-0f15-4128-8b92-8e7ed9bcc3ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Workflow pain point"}, {"id": "69ef296f-ae88-4450-bf7e-fd18efa1e0a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety or quality gap"}, {"id": "483fb1d3-995b-4bca-b2bd-d2c25fc81600", "type": "concept", "title": "Patient access or equity concern"}]}, {"id": "7bcaf8d5-9d7e-460a-a1a4-5cd7d4b08b98", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evaluation design", "description": "Students compare technology against evidence and implementation reality.", "children": [{"id": "c91ca4bb-289a-4286-afe0-469dee8e5e79", "type": "concept", "title": "Stakeholders, requirements, risks, and constraints"}, {"id": "c0445d13-bfd5-4688-af15-2752f9351d6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Data, workflow, privacy, and equity criteria"}, {"id": "68922f16-cc3f-4131-8747-99e4932a1f06", "type": "concept", "title": "Outcome and process measures"}]}, {"id": "9e427d8b-5ed9-453b-9c2d-0ef0ad82ddd1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Executive recommendation", "description": "The final product should be useful to a nurse leader or implementation team.", "children": [{"id": "d084120f-2c6f-4c2d-97d9-dc09baca9128", "type": "concept", "title": "Recommendation memo"}, {"id": "f4711f36-2471-48f4-9522-6c348a476821", "type": "concept", "title": "Implementation roadmap"}, {"id": "4b446553-45aa-4c93-8e95-e88be53c7711", "type": "concept", "title": "Dashboard sketch and evaluation plan"}]}]}], "dbBacked": true}$nihtjson$::jsonb,
